## 2026-05-22T00:24:18Z - commit 07 / kernel derive add value config output derives

- Summary: Implemented `mfm-program-derive` derives for `MfmValue`, `MfmConfig`, `StateInput`, `OperationOutput`, and `PublicOutputs`; added `StateInput`, `OperationOutput`, and `PublicOutputs` descriptor contracts to `mfm-values`; added derive-backed descriptor golden tests; added trybuild pass/fail fixtures covering downstream derives, unsupported serde attributes, floats, `serde_json::Value`, `HashMap`, skipped fields, custom serializers/defaults, known secret wrappers, and manual impl attempts. Also implemented the planned manual persisted-trait source-boundary checker and wired it into `nix run .#check` / CI summary output with `manual_value_config_output_impls_rejected`.
- Tests run and results: `cargo test -p mfm-program-derive` passed; `cargo clippy -p mfm-program-derive --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed; `cargo test -p mfm-values` passed; `cargo clippy -p mfm-values --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed; `nixfied/project/check-manual-persisted-impls.sh --root . --self-test --summary-file /tmp/mfm-manual-impl-summary.json` passed and produced `manual_value_config_output_impls_rejected=true`; `git diff --check` passed; `nix run .#check` passed; `nix run .#test` passed.
- Design decisions: Kept derives limited to named, non-generic structs in v1. Derives generate schema descriptors only and no scheduling/runtime logic. `serde(rename)` and supported `rename_all` forms resolve to concrete wire names; unsupported serde controls fail compile-time. `serde(default)` emits an `MfmDefault` bound instead of trusting `Default`. Floats, `usize`/`isize`, `HashMap`, raw `serde_json::Value`, and known secret wrappers including `Zeroizing` are rejected before descriptor generation. `MfmValue` semantic ids are derived from checked semantic identity fields at macro expansion time. Trybuild output is directed to a temp target dir so generated Cargo manifests do not pollute discovery artifacts. The manual-impl checker is parser-based rather than regex-based and rejects authored persisted trait impls and `__derive_generated` provenance calls outside framework allowlists, including alias and multiline forms.
- Doubts, risks, blockers, or review items: First validator pass found P1 issues that derive provenance was forgeable through the public hidden constructor and manual impl fixtures only covered one trait. Added source-boundary enforcement plus full manual-impl fixtures. Second validator pass found P1 bypasses in the regex checker through aliases and multiline impls. Replaced it with a Rust tokenizer/parser checker and added self-tests for aliased multiline manual impls and aliased forged provenance. Final re-review reported no remaining P0/P1 findings. Residual P2/P3 risks: source-boundary enforcement does not inspect generated code from build scripts/proc macros, alias tracking is repository-global and can conservatively false-positive future aliases, and self-tests cover alias/multiline behavior with one persisted-trait exemplar while the shared trait list applies the logic to all six traits.

